From 24ab4c546bef5fcdabbd368a7f43f5b416331743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CompuLab <support@compulab.co.il>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:25:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: tegra: support ADI stream-aware SerDes pipelines

Traverse the active V4L2 route for the selected CSI virtual channel instead
of assuming that the previous media pad is the upstream sink. Retain the
sensor as the NVIDIA metadata and control provider, associate it with the
linked NVCSI channel, and propagate its format through bridge state.

Start NVCSI first, then request the selected stream from the first bridge.
The ADI bridge recursively starts its serializer and sensor, so do not call
those upstream subdevices a second time. Preserve the existing s_stream
path for ordinary sensor pipelines and roll back downstream startup if a
stream-aware bridge fails.

Respect Maxim child async notifiers, resolve their subdevices after root
completion, reuse their immutable media links, and match each shared
bridge output by endpoint. Find the physical I2C controller through nested
gates/address translators when constructing NVIDIA sensor metadata.

Add an optional sensor get_frame_desc callback to camera_common_sensor_ops
and forward it from the stock tegracam pad operations before registration.
The EDGEDES sensor modules supply their native CSI datatype and VC there.

Initialize optional private sensor controls and per-instance pad operations
before async publication, so VI copies a complete control handler and the
subdevice uses the sensor's final lock from its first bind.

Zero legacy pad-operation requests to select stream 0 under Linux 6.18.
Bound the control-copy traversal before reading the next subdevice because
NVCSI, deserializer, serializer and sensor consume all four array slots.
Avoid changing bridge formats that already match an active route.

Prepared against the unmodified NVIDIA Jetson Linux 39.2.1 public source.
This integration targets the Linux 6.18 V4L2 Streams API.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NVIDIA tegracam and CompuLab EDGEDES integration]
Signed-off-by: CompuLab <support@compulab.co.il>
